 "summary": "Interference reported a board lying wholly in the open cavity of a watch case as inside the case once the case's outer top rim (a full circle) was filleted: the case-board intersection kept the whole board. SolidCraft reported the issue and its fix in the same PR, so `issue` is that PR's conversation. The case is a r 25 cylinder from z 1.5 to 15.8 with its top rim rounded r 1.5 and an open r 21.5 cavity cut up to z 13.2 from below. The boards are thin, so SolidCraft meshed both bodies finely (the case in about 180 000 triangles), its sampled 'apart' shortcut gave up, and a shifted retry of the numerical intersection kept the whole board. Geometry is the PR tests': the kernel test's 0.2 mm board, and the engine test's 1 mm board and pad (the reported 750 mm3 and 35.95 mm3). Every board corner lies at r 19.85, inside the cavity.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "thin_board_in_cavity",
   "note": "the kernel test: a 0.2 mm board; SolidCraft's failing retry returned the whole board (150 mm3)",
   "steps": [
    {
     "op": "cylinder",
     "id": "outer",
     "origin": [
      0,
      0,
      1.5
     ],
     "radius": 25,
     "height": 14.3
    },
    {
     "op": "fillet",
     "id": "rounded",
     "body": "outer",
     "edges": [
      [
       25,
       0,
       15.8
      ]
     ],
     "radius": 1.5
    },
    {
     "op": "cylinder",
     "id": "cavity",
     "origin": [
      0,
      0,
      1.5
     ],
     "radius": 21.5,
     "height": 11.7
    },
    {
     "op": "difference",
     "id": "case",
     "a": "rounded",
     "b": "cavity"
    },
    {
     "op": "box",
     "id": "tool",
     "origin": [
      -12,
      -15,
      6.9
     ],
     "size": [
      25,
      30,
      0.2
     ]
    },
    {
     "op": "intersection",
     "id": "result",
     "a": "case",
     "b": "tool"
    }
   ],
   "expect": {
    "lumps": 0,
    "volume": {
     "value": 0,
     "tol": 0.001,
     "formula": "0: the bodies share no volume"
    }
   }
